IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fta-types`
IMPORT `fta-conduct`
IMPORT `fta-transactions`
IMPORT `fta-safety`
IMPORT `fta-enforcement`
IMPORT `fta-goal`

-- Independent tests for the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ) encoding.
-- Expected values come from independent-expectations.md, written from the
-- statute before the encoding was read. Scenario ids (A1, G3, ...) refer to it.
-- A failing assertion is a finding; expected values are never changed to fit.

§ `Calendars`

-- Labour Day 2026, Easter 2026, and 25 Dec 2026 - 1 Jan 2027.
`calendar 2026` MEANS `Working day calendar` OF (LIST (Date 3 4 2026), (Date 6 4 2026), (Date 26 10 2026), (Date 25 12 2026), (Date 28 12 2026), (Date 29 12 2026), (Date 30 12 2026), (Date 31 12 2026), (Date 1 1 2027))

`no holidays` MEANS `Working day calendar` OF EMPTY

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN p IS A Prohibition, q IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`a case of` p q t k MEANS `Conduct case` OF p, q, t, k, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (Date 15 10 2023)

GIVEN p IS A Prohibition, t IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`a crown case of` p t MEANS `Conduct case` OF p, TRUE, t, `a body corporate`, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (Date 15 10 2023)

GIVEN p IS A Prohibition, m IS A `News media facts`
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`a media case of` p m MEANS `Conduct case` OF p, TRUE, TRUE, `a body corporate`, FALSE, (JUST m), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (Date 15 10 2023)

GIVEN p IS A Prohibition, k IS A `Contracting out clause`
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`a contracted case of` p k MEANS `Conduct case` OF p, TRUE, TRUE, `a body corporate`, FALSE, NOTHING, (JUST k), FALSE, FALSE, (Date 15 10 2023)

GIVEN r IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`an unsubstantiated case of` r e MEANS `Conduct case` OF `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`, TRUE, TRUE, `a body corporate`, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, r, e, (Date 15 10 2023)

GIVEN c IS A `Conduct case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`contravenes` c MEANS `the conduct contravenes the provision` c

GIVEN c IS A `Conduct case`
GIVETH A `Fair trading position`
`position` c MEANS `the fair trading position for` c

`a valid clause` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§ `A. In trade`

-- A1, A2, A3
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 7 unconscionable conduct in trade` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 7 unconscionable conduct in trade` TRUE TRUE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A4, A5
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` TRUE TRUE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A6
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 10 conduct liable to mislead the public about goods` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 11 conduct liable to mislead the public about services` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
-- A7
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 12 misleading conduct about employment` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A8, A9, A10
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 14(1) a false or misleading representation about land` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
-- A11
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 14(2) force, harassment or coercion about land` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A12, A13, A14
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 16 forging or falsely applying a trade mark` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 17 offering gifts or prizes not intended to be provided` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 19 bait advertising` TRUE TRUE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A15, A17
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 20 referral selling` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 21 accepting payment without intending to supply` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A18
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 21C asserting a right to payment for unsolicited goods or services` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
-- A19, A20, A21, A22
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 22 misleading representations about business activities` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 23 harassment or coercion` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 24 promoting or operating a pyramid selling scheme` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 26A or 26B using an unfair contract term` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- A23: s 32 notices and the s 32(5) prohibition are limited to supply "in trade".
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 32 a compulsory recall notice` TRUE FALSE `a body corporate`) EQUALS FALSE
-- A25
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 36RA entering or not leaving residential premises` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 31 supplying goods under an unsafe goods notice` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS TRUE
-- conduct without the quality never contravenes
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` FALSE TRUE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE
-- L10: gift card sold not in trade
#ASSERT contravenes (`a case of` `s 36WB a gift card expiring in less than 3 years` TRUE FALSE `an individual`) EQUALS FALSE

§ `B. The Crown`

-- B1, B2
#ASSERT contravenes (`a crown case of` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a crown case of` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT contravenes (`a crown case of` `s 12 misleading conduct about employment` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- B3 / O26: Crown in trade contravenes s 13 but cannot be prosecuted
#ASSERT (position (`a crown case of` `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services` TRUE))'s `the conduct contravenes the Act` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (position (`a crown case of` `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services` TRUE))'s `it is an offence` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the maximum fine for contravening` `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services` `, by` `a body corporate` `, the Crown:` TRUE EQUALS 0

